      "math_academy_id": "e-6097",
      "problem": "Evaluate the repeated integral $\\displaystyle \\int_{2}^{4}  \\int_{0}^{2} \\dfrac{x^3}{y^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x  \\, \\textrm{d}y.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}(\\frac{{2}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{0}^{4}}{4})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{4}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =4{[-\\frac{1}{y}]}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =4(-\\frac{1}{4}-(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
